flowchart TB
    admin[Ordinary authenticated Admin domain edit]
    adminTx[BEGIN IMMEDIATE\ncheck expected_revision\nvalidate complete next TeamState\ncommit next revision]
    conflict[409 conflict\nreload and merge]

    mcp[Team MCP command]
    identity[Resolve ambient session\nagent, governance, or assignment scope\nactive lease and stand-down]
    replay{request_id already stored?}
    same[Return original stored response]
    different[Idempotency conflict\nno domain mutation]
    commandTx[One BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction\nvalidate command and inbox IDs\nmutate TeamState and revision\nappend dispatch activity\ninsert or reuse outbox rows\nstore idempotent response]

    db[(Team SQLite)]
    outbox[(team_outbox\nin the same SQLite commit)]
    publisher[Outbox publisher\nclaim, publish, complete or retry]
    workflow[Core workflow runtime]
    effect[Wake, spawn, Git, release,\nor communication effect]

    admin --> adminTx
    adminTx -- stale revision --> conflict
    adminTx -- current revision --> db

    mcp --> identity --> replay
    replay -- same payload --> same
    replay -- different payload --> different
    replay -- new request --> commandTx
    commandTx --> db
    commandTx -. atomic with state and activity .-> outbox
    outbox --> publisher --> workflow --> effect

    distinction[Ordinary Admin domain edits use expected_revision.\nAppend-only Chat validates its current conversation instead.\nMCP commands use ambient identity, dispatch scope, and request_id.]
    distinction --- admin
    distinction --- mcp
